WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.890
Night in London.

2
00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:05.700
A small, hunched man
hurries under the gas lamps.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.920
Everyone who meets him
struggles to describe him.

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.970
A lawyer wonders: "Something troglodytic,

5
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.270
shall we say?"

6
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.410
A butler calls him "that
masked thing like a monkey".

7
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.410
Why does everyone reach for animal words?

8
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.800
In this mission, you'll meet
Darwin's big idea from 1859,

9
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.990
and ask what it made some
Victorians afraid of.

10
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.520
You'll collect the animal
words, from a lawyer,

11
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.100
a butler, and Jekyll himself.

12
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.400
And you'll walk two
Londons: grand squares,

13
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.440
and "The dismal quarter of Soho".

14
00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:44.530
Your mission: explain why so many
characters describe Hyde like an animal.
